      "message": "Pool count omits an Assignment.active filter. terminate_assignment() sets active\u003dFalse but only rewinds current-window rows, leaving future-dated self-schedule rows (admin\nbatch with future dates, or PATCH moving a window forward) on the dead assignment.\n\nThose stale rows still count here, so a terminated assignment falsely consumes pool slots:\nfree hosts get rejected with \"reached its self-scheduling limit\" and capped out of the can_self_schedule\u003dtrue listing. Same omission ab3dc63 (#746) just fixed in\nget_current_schedule. Suggest .filter(Assignment.active.is_(True)).",
